WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.722
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:12.992 --> 00:15.995
Your daughter is 4 now, right?

3
00:16.079 --> 00:16.955
Yes.

4
00:17.497 --> 00:20.542
She doesn't react even when her mother talks to her?

5
00:21.334 --> 00:22.627
My wife…

6
00:22.710 --> 00:25.797
Passed away when she was 1.

7
00:31.302 --> 00:32.303
Minami.

8
00:34.013 --> 00:35.014
Minami.

9
00:36.141 --> 00:37.767
Minami Minamida.

10
00:44.899 --> 00:47.151
It's great that you got a toy.

11
00:48.152 --> 00:49.070
Do you like it?

12
00:50.530 --> 00:51.823
Hey, Minami.

13
00:53.157 --> 00:55.743
Do you know who Dad is?

14
01:14.804 --> 01:16.764
My name is Minami Minamida.

15
01:17.390 --> 01:20.476
Read forwards or backwards, it's Minami Minamida.

16
01:21.102 --> 01:24.647
Kayak, deed, rotator, civic, racecar, Minami Minamida.

17
01:45.084 --> 01:47.587
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR NEW JOB

18
01:57.180 --> 01:59.557
MINAMI'S DAD MAKOTO MINAMIDA

19
02:01.267 --> 02:02.518
Good morning.

20
02:02.602 --> 02:03.603
Morning.

21
02:06.481 --> 02:09.734
It will be sunny over a wide area today, perfect for going out.

22
02:09.817 --> 02:13.404
Tokyo's estimated high is 21 degrees.

23
02:13.488 --> 02:16.866
The estimated low is 17 degrees. Perf--

24
02:17.909 --> 02:19.827
The estimated high is 21 degrees.

25
02:19.911 --> 02:22.121
The estimated low is 17 degrees.

26
02:23.748 --> 02:26.626
Minami, it looks good on you.

27
02:31.130 --> 02:33.383
That's your gift from Dad for your new job.

28
02:33.466 --> 02:34.425
How is it? Happy?

29
02:36.052 --> 02:37.804
I'm very happy.

30
02:37.887 --> 02:39.764
Minami, no.

31
02:45.353 --> 02:46.229
Here.

32
02:47.730 --> 02:50.525
This is the "happy" face.

33
02:50.608 --> 02:52.652
HAPPY

34
02:55.738 --> 02:56.572
Like this?

35
02:57.156 --> 02:59.367
Yes! You look happy.

36
03:02.120 --> 03:04.831
Here is the Minami Minamida set. Here you go.

37
03:07.208 --> 03:08.209
Let's eat.

38
03:19.053 --> 03:21.723
I always eat salted rice balls for my meals.

39
03:22.390 --> 03:24.308
Salted rice balls are safe.

40
03:24.392 --> 03:26.936
Since they only contain salt and rice,

41
03:27.020 --> 03:29.272
I'm not surprised by unexpected flavors.

42
03:32.066 --> 03:33.151
Listen, Minami.

43
03:34.110 --> 03:35.945
No parroting at work.

44
03:36.029 --> 03:38.323
And don't say anything unnecessary in your introduction.

45
03:39.032 --> 03:40.825
Don't be too honest, either.

46
03:41.951 --> 03:45.163
Echolalia, needless details, and total honesty are forbidden.

47
03:45.955 --> 03:46.956
And whatever you do,

48
03:47.582 --> 03:49.125
don't talk about whales.

49
03:52.170 --> 03:54.213
What if we need to talk about whales?

50
03:54.297 --> 03:56.507
Is your workplace Kamogawa Sea World?

51
03:57.175 --> 03:58.926
That'll never come up.

52
03:59.010 --> 04:01.471
But what if it becomes absolutely necessary,

53
04:01.554 --> 04:04.474
and everyone except me is talking about nothing but whales?

54
04:05.641 --> 04:08.102
Then it's fine.

55
04:08.186 --> 04:09.270
Okay!

56
04:12.440 --> 04:13.608
Thank you for the meal.

57
04:16.027 --> 04:17.362
Are you leaving already?

58
04:17.445 --> 04:18.946
Your lunch box is in your bag.

59
04:19.781 --> 04:20.948
Thank you.

60
04:25.870 --> 04:27.955
I'll be going now.

61
04:28.039 --> 04:28.915
Take care.

62
04:30.208 --> 04:31.334
Eat your side dishes, too.

63
04:44.847 --> 04:46.557
AN AUTISTIC ATTORNEY IS BORN!

64
04:46.641 --> 04:49.185
HIROKAWA &amp; HOWARD LPC MINAMI MINAMIDA

65
04:49.268 --> 04:51.604
HER FATHER MAKOTO, ALWAYS BY HER SIDE

66
05:00.738 --> 05:04.367
I don't like the morning commute because there are too many people.

67
05:08.162 --> 05:09.414
At times like this,

68
05:09.497 --> 05:12.333
I try to imagine whales swimming freely in the ocean.

69
05:31.519 --> 05:33.229
Whales are fascinating.

70
05:33.813 --> 05:37.191
They're said to sense the earth's magnetic field,

71
05:37.275 --> 05:39.694
and can migrate thousands of miles

72
05:39.777 --> 05:43.406
in that vast ocean without getting lost.

73
05:49.370 --> 05:50.955
What awaits me

74
05:51.038 --> 05:52.790
as I sail this ocean?

75
06:23.321 --> 06:24.947
ELEVATOR UNDER CONSTRUCTION

76
07:02.485 --> 07:03.569
Excuse me.

77
07:08.449 --> 07:09.450
I'm sorry.

78
07:18.709 --> 07:20.002
PARALEGAL MINATO FUNAI

79
07:20.086 --> 07:21.837
Shall I show you to the stairs?

80
07:24.799 --> 07:27.260
It's a bit hard to find your way to the reception

81
07:27.343 --> 07:29.470
from the emergency stairs in this building.

82
07:30.596 --> 07:31.973
Where are you headed?

83
07:32.765 --> 07:34.767
Hirokawa &amp; Howard LPC.

84
07:35.726 --> 07:37.228
Then we're on the same floor.

85
07:37.311 --> 07:39.272
Do you have an appointment with someone?

86
07:39.355 --> 07:41.148
I have an appointment with Mr. Miyaji.

87
07:42.108 --> 07:43.276
Good morning.

88
07:44.360 --> 07:47.363
HIROKAWA &amp; HOWARD LPC

89
07:55.037 --> 07:57.540
Here it is. Mr. Miyaji's office.

90
07:57.623 --> 07:59.125
Well, I'll leave you here.

91
07:59.208 --> 08:00.626
Thank you very much.

92
08:01.544 --> 08:02.545
You're welcome.

93
08:11.095 --> 08:12.263
Come in.

94
08:13.347 --> 08:14.432
Excuse me.

95
08:27.945 --> 08:28.779
ATTORNEY KOHARU ASAHI

96
08:28.863 --> 08:30.448
May I ask who you are?

97
08:31.198 --> 08:33.534
I'm Minami Minamida, and I'll be working here

98
08:33.618 --> 08:35.328
as an attorney starting today.

99
08:35.411 --> 08:36.245
PARTNER KENGO MIYAJI

100
08:36.329 --> 08:37.455
Is it that time already?

101
08:37.538 --> 08:38.372
ATTORNEY TAKUMA HIMI

102
08:38.456 --> 08:39.582
A new hire right now?

103
08:39.665 --> 08:41.292
She's six months behind you two.

104
08:42.209 --> 08:44.503
RESUME MINAMI MINAMIDA

105
08:44.587 --> 08:47.757
Well, she graduated top of her class from Tokyo University,

106
08:47.840 --> 08:50.843
and ranked first in the bar exam.

107
08:51.886 --> 08:53.596
You're quite outstanding.

108
08:54.096 --> 08:56.474
Have you seen the second page of my resume?

109
08:59.602 --> 09:02.730
I wrote Autism Spectrum Disorder on the second page.

110
09:02.813 --> 09:04.106
Autism Spectrum Disorder?

111
09:04.190 --> 09:06.942
Autism Spectrum Disorder is a developmental disorder.

112
09:07.026 --> 09:08.402
Due to atypical brain function,

113
09:08.486 --> 09:09.862
social communication

114
09:09.945 --> 09:11.155
can be difficult--

115
09:11.238 --> 09:12.406
I know what it is.

116
09:13.282 --> 09:14.825
I see.

117
09:14.909 --> 09:16.452
Any other special notes?

118
09:17.453 --> 09:18.287
What?

119
09:18.371 --> 09:21.707
Read forwards or backwards, my name is Minami Minamida.

120
09:21.791 --> 09:24.669
Kayak, deed, rotator, civic, racecar, Minami Minamida.

121
09:28.964 --> 09:31.217
Wait, it's today, right? You know, that thing.

122
09:31.300 --> 09:33.469
I need to go for a bit. I'm sorry,

123
09:33.552 --> 09:35.846
but could you two handle the greetings and stuff?

124
09:35.930 --> 09:36.889
What?

125
09:39.392 --> 09:42.561
Ms. Minamida, you can't do that at work.

126
09:42.645 --> 09:45.731
The instructors warned you about the kayak and racecar stuff.

127
09:45.815 --> 09:49.235
I can't do that at work. Kayaks and racecars are forbidden.

128
09:49.318 --> 09:51.112
But I can't help but say them.

129
09:51.195 --> 09:53.864
What? Ms. Asahi, do you know her?

130
09:53.948 --> 09:55.783
We were legal trainees together.

131
09:56.409 --> 09:58.202
Look, you have bedhead again.

132
10:00.788 --> 10:03.332
I'm surprised you got in. How did you get in?

133
10:03.874 --> 10:05.209
The same as everyone else.

134
10:05.292 --> 10:07.044
Through the automatic front doors.

135
10:10.172 --> 10:11.257
PARTNER NAGISA HIROKAWA

136
10:11.340 --> 10:12.258
Come in.

137
10:14.719 --> 10:16.637
Mr. Miyaji is here.

138
10:16.721 --> 10:17.972
SECRETARY KAEDE TSUCHIMURA

139
10:20.558 --> 10:22.685
The rookie you hired has arrived.

140
10:22.768 --> 10:23.602
I see.

141
10:23.686 --> 10:26.439
There's a second page to this resume.

142
10:26.522 --> 10:28.357
It says she has autism.

143
10:28.941 --> 10:29.817
Yes.

144
10:30.526 --> 10:32.027
Why hire her knowing…

145
10:32.862 --> 10:34.363
Her background isn't bad.

146
10:35.156 --> 10:36.991
Doesn't she just have a good memory?

147
10:37.074 --> 10:39.493
I don't think someone who can't introduce herself properly

148
10:39.577 --> 10:41.078
is fit for the job.

149
10:41.162 --> 10:42.371
Then, maybe,

150
10:42.872 --> 10:45.666
I should ask my father about how excellent you were

151
10:45.750 --> 10:47.084
when you were a rookie.

152
10:47.168 --> 10:48.043
That's…

153
10:50.838 --> 10:51.839
Understood.

154
10:52.923 --> 10:54.258
If you say so,

155
10:54.341 --> 10:56.343
I'll entrust her with one case.

156
10:56.844 --> 11:00.055
If she isn't at the level to stand in court,

157
11:00.139 --> 11:01.974
will you reconsider her employment?

158
11:02.808 --> 11:03.726
Yes.

159
11:04.518 --> 11:05.352
Fair enough.

160
11:05.436 --> 11:06.395
Excuse me then.

161
11:15.905 --> 11:18.741
MINAMIDA, BORN DEC. 20, 2002 (23) 4-4-1 MIDORIGAOKA, NAKANO, TOKYO

162
11:20.493 --> 11:22.328
Well then, let's start the meeting.

163
11:22.411 --> 11:25.456
This time, I'm thinking of having you handle a criminal case

164
11:25.539 --> 11:27.666
instead of a civil one…

165
11:29.210 --> 11:30.419
Ms. Minamida.

166
11:31.086 --> 11:31.921
Yes.

167
11:32.004 --> 11:33.464
Can I ask you something?

168
11:34.048 --> 11:36.258
Why did you become a lawyer?

169
11:37.510 --> 11:41.138
Because I passed the bar exam. Is it different for you, Mr. Miyaji?

170
11:42.223 --> 11:43.974
I'm asking about your reason or motivation.

171
11:45.184 --> 11:46.185
Motivation?

172
11:50.397 --> 11:51.732
Never mind.

173
11:52.233 --> 11:55.236
The defendant is a 72-year-old woman.

174
11:55.778 --> 11:59.240
She was caring for her husband because he had dementia,

175
11:59.323 --> 12:01.116
but they got into a fight that day.

176
12:01.659 --> 12:05.663
Angered by his insults, she hit his head.

177
12:06.330 --> 12:09.250
Yes, that's right, with the iron that was nearby.

178
12:09.333 --> 12:10.626
With the nearby iron.

179
12:17.424 --> 12:20.219
This iron looks just like a sperm whale.

180
12:20.302 --> 12:21.804
A sperm whale?

181
12:22.513 --> 12:25.432
Yes. Their spermaceti organ holds wax-like liquid

182
12:25.516 --> 12:27.851
to produce sound waves.

183
12:27.935 --> 12:29.270
Yes, I understand.

184
12:29.353 --> 12:30.312
-Moving on-- -Have you

185
12:30.396 --> 12:32.022
seen the animated film Pinocchio?

186
12:32.106 --> 12:33.732
The whale that appears in the climax

187
12:33.816 --> 12:35.192
is modeled after a sperm whale

188
12:35.276 --> 12:36.986
due to its square-shaped head,

189
12:37.069 --> 12:38.195
but real sperm whales

190
12:38.279 --> 12:39.989
have hidden teeth in their upper jaw--

191
12:40.072 --> 12:42.324
-What is this about? -Sperm whales.

192
12:44.577 --> 12:46.036
Please focus.

193
12:46.996 --> 12:48.038
I'm sorry.

194
12:48.956 --> 12:50.624
Whale talk is forbidden.

195
12:56.714 --> 12:59.174
Hey, a package arrived.

196
12:59.258 --> 13:00.259
You sign for it.

197
13:02.136 --> 13:04.847
The least you could do is grab it.

198
13:08.100 --> 13:09.560
Thanks for your hard work.

199
13:09.643 --> 13:11.061
-A signature, right? -Thank you.

200
13:11.145 --> 13:12.313
Can you put it here?

201
13:12.396 --> 13:13.480
Sure.

202
13:13.564 --> 13:16.191
-Wasn't it heavy? -No, not at all.

203
13:16.817 --> 13:17.901
Thanks a lot.

204
13:18.402 --> 13:19.570
Anytime.

205
13:19.653 --> 13:23.324
You're nice and seem earnest.

206
13:23.407 --> 13:24.992
You'd make a good husband.

207
13:25.951 --> 13:27.286
Seriously, what the hell?

208
13:27.369 --> 13:30.205
Flirting with another man in the middle of the day!

209
13:30.706 --> 13:31.957
Please don't mind him.

210
13:32.750 --> 13:34.335
Thanks for the delivery.

211
13:34.418 --> 13:35.544
Thank you.

212
13:37.671 --> 13:38.672
Have a good day.

213
13:44.595 --> 13:45.804
Stop it.

214
13:46.388 --> 13:47.848
He could be my grandson.

215
13:47.931 --> 13:50.934
You have a husband, yet you flirt with other men.

216
13:51.018 --> 13:52.144
Don't say that.

217
13:52.227 --> 13:55.981
You're just hoping I die soon!

218
14:02.237 --> 14:03.781
Why would you do that?

219
14:04.365 --> 14:05.866
I'm the one who has to clean it up!

220
14:05.949 --> 14:07.534
Don't act all high and mighty

221
14:07.618 --> 14:09.411
just because you clean.

222
14:11.121 --> 14:12.915
I can't take this anymore.

223
14:15.542 --> 14:16.377
What?

224
14:16.460 --> 14:17.586
Let's die.

225
14:19.338 --> 14:20.547
Let's die together…

226
14:21.799 --> 14:22.967
And end this!

227
14:23.050 --> 14:24.385
Stop! Stop!

228
14:25.719 --> 14:27.429
I'll kill you…

229
14:28.514 --> 14:30.224
And then I'll die too!

230
14:30.307 --> 14:32.309
This is the end.

231
14:40.693 --> 14:41.819
Dear?

232
14:41.902 --> 14:42.861
No!

233
14:44.780 --> 14:45.823
Wake up!

234
14:45.906 --> 14:47.950
Wake up, dear!

235
14:48.033 --> 14:48.909
KEIKO ICHINOSE

236
14:48.993 --> 14:51.745
The husband suffered a subdural hematoma with a 12-week recovery.

237
14:51.829 --> 14:53.288
Wife charged with attempted murder.

238
14:53.372 --> 14:54.790
Wife charged with attempted murder.

239
14:54.873 --> 14:56.542
H-- Hey…

240
14:57.418 --> 14:58.669
Why are you repeating me?

241
15:00.838 --> 15:01.922
I'm sorry.

242
15:02.006 --> 15:03.590
Echolalia is forbidden!

243
15:03.674 --> 15:04.717
Echolalia?

244
15:05.968 --> 15:07.469
It means parroting words.

245
15:07.553 --> 15:09.179
It's a trait of autism.

246
15:10.014 --> 15:11.557
Let's drop the echolalia then.

247
15:11.640 --> 15:13.142
Let's drop the echolalia then.

248
15:15.644 --> 15:16.895
Anyway…

249
15:16.979 --> 15:18.522
Wife charged with attempted murder.

250
15:18.605 --> 15:20.733
But fortunately, no request for detention was made.

251
15:21.275 --> 15:23.027
Even though it's attempted murder?

252
15:23.110 --> 15:25.237
The prosecution is sympathetic, too.

253
15:25.320 --> 15:26.905
The defendant herself is in her 70s,

254
15:26.989 --> 15:30.117
yet she's been caring for her husband in his 80s with dementia.

255
15:31.452 --> 15:32.327
Now,

256
15:32.828 --> 15:37.332
Ms. Minamida, what should you do for this defendant?

257
15:39.626 --> 15:41.086
Get her a suspended sentence.

258
15:41.170 --> 15:44.173
Despite the charge, it's very possible here.

259
15:50.596 --> 15:52.431
Hello. I'm Minami Minamida.

260
15:53.223 --> 15:54.433
I will do my absolute best!

261
15:57.227 --> 15:58.228
What about you?

262
15:58.854 --> 16:02.066
I will be defending you as well, of course, but she will be in charge.

263
16:05.069 --> 16:07.362
I was very surprised when I looked at the files.

264
16:08.072 --> 16:10.365
I lived there until 19 years ago, too.

265
16:10.449 --> 16:11.867
In that apartment in Nishikasai.

266
16:12.868 --> 16:15.287
Ocean Heim Nishikasai, Unit 202.

267
16:15.913 --> 16:18.791
It's the unit right next to yours, Ms. Ichinose.

268
16:18.874 --> 16:19.708
Really?

269
16:19.792 --> 16:21.877
I remembered the name of the building.

270
16:21.960 --> 16:24.046
Read forwards or backwards,

271
16:24.129 --> 16:27.382
202 and the kanji for Nishikasai read the same.

272
16:27.466 --> 16:28.300
MINAMI MINAMIDA

273
16:28.383 --> 16:29.802
Minami Minamida…

274
16:31.220 --> 16:32.930
Are you that Little Minami?

275
16:33.013 --> 16:34.598
Do you know her?

276
16:36.016 --> 16:41.480
Little Minami really became a lawyer!

277
16:41.563 --> 16:43.482
Isn't that amazing?

278
16:44.983 --> 16:46.401
Well, I'm going to head out.

279
16:46.485 --> 16:48.570
You can hear the rest directly from her.

280
16:49.279 --> 16:50.239
I'll take my leave.

281
16:50.322 --> 16:55.160
It's truly amazing. You worked so hard, Minami!

282
16:55.244 --> 16:58.247
STATEMENT OF PLANNED DEFENSE

283
17:03.335 --> 17:04.169
What is this?

284
17:04.253 --> 17:06.338
It's the defense's planned defense statement.

285
17:06.421 --> 17:07.339
I know that.

286
17:07.422 --> 17:08.924
But it says "not guilty" here?

287
17:09.007 --> 17:12.094
I intend to plead not guilty to the charge of attempted murder.

288
17:12.845 --> 17:14.930
No matter how big our firm is,

289
17:15.013 --> 17:16.557
there are things we can and cannot do.

290
17:16.640 --> 17:19.017
But she should be found not guilty of attempted murder.

291
17:19.101 --> 17:20.477
I told you, didn't I?

292
17:20.561 --> 17:23.313
Get a suspended sentence, which is fine for this case.

293
17:23.397 --> 17:25.107
But that's not good enough.

294
17:25.190 --> 17:26.275
Why not?

295
17:27.943 --> 17:29.611
This case is interesting.

296
17:29.695 --> 17:31.613
It's like one of my favorite whale riddles.

297
17:31.697 --> 17:34.158
-Excuse me? -When a 22-ton sperm whale

298
17:34.241 --> 17:35.826
eats a 500-kilogram giant squid

299
17:35.909 --> 17:38.370
and lays a 1.3-ton egg six hours later,

300
17:38.453 --> 17:40.497
how many tons does the sperm whale weigh?

301
17:40.581 --> 17:41.415
I have no idea.

302
17:41.498 --> 17:44.418
The correct answer is, "Whales don't lay eggs."

303
17:44.501 --> 17:46.879
If you focus on the weight, you can't find the answer.

304
17:46.962 --> 17:47.796
You'll miss it.

305
17:47.880 --> 17:49.006
And?

306
17:49.089 --> 17:49.923
This case

307
17:50.007 --> 17:53.135
is a criminal case, so people tend to focus on criminal law.

308
17:53.218 --> 17:54.887
But that won't give you the answer.

309
17:54.970 --> 17:56.555
The answer is in civil law.

310
17:56.638 --> 17:59.766
-Civil law? -Civil Code Article 891, Item 1 stipulates

311
17:59.850 --> 18:01.518
that you cannot inherit

312
18:01.602 --> 18:03.812
the assets of someone you tried to kill.

313
18:03.896 --> 18:04.897
Inheritance…

314
18:04.980 --> 18:08.317
The defendant currently lives mainly off her husband's pension.

315
18:08.400 --> 18:10.694
If she's found guilty of attempted murder,

316
18:10.777 --> 18:14.031
she may lose his pension

317
18:14.114 --> 18:16.742
and inheritance after he passes,

318
18:16.825 --> 18:18.327
leaving her destitute.

319
18:18.410 --> 18:20.412
Therefore, I will get her a suspended sentence

320
18:20.495 --> 18:22.497
for bodily injury, not attempted murder.

321
18:28.253 --> 18:30.923
Were you testing her to see if she'd notice

322
18:31.006 --> 18:32.591
the hidden issue in this case?

323
18:32.674 --> 18:33.508
No.

324
18:34.259 --> 18:35.761
I hadn't noticed it.

325
18:36.428 --> 18:38.597
There was a hint in her statement.

326
18:39.598 --> 18:41.433
On page 24, line 7, it says,

327
18:41.516 --> 18:44.478
"Five years ago, I quit my part-time cleaning job

328
18:44.561 --> 18:47.064
to focus on caring for my husband."

329
18:47.147 --> 18:48.482
That's what it says.

330
18:48.565 --> 18:49.942
Remembering that,

331
18:50.025 --> 18:51.652
I checked her finances.

332
18:51.735 --> 18:52.653
QUIT MY PART-TIME JOB

333
18:52.736 --> 18:54.446
Ms. Minamida, that's brilliant.

334
18:54.529 --> 18:57.574
Even a normal lawyer wouldn't easily catch that.

335
19:02.120 --> 19:02.955
What is it?

336
19:03.038 --> 19:04.206
I'm sorry.

337
19:05.666 --> 19:09.086
Saying "normal lawyer" was rude.

338
19:12.506 --> 19:13.966
Please don't worry about it.

339
19:14.049 --> 19:16.260
Because I'm not a normal lawyer.

340
19:18.845 --> 19:20.806
Who exactly is Ms. Minamida?

341
19:21.515 --> 19:23.725
Why did the Managing Partner hire her now?

342
19:25.018 --> 19:25.936
Beats me.

343
19:26.019 --> 19:28.313
Was she like that during the legal training too?

344
19:28.397 --> 19:30.190
Do you want to hear about it?

345
19:30.899 --> 19:32.442
Like the time she finished

346
19:32.526 --> 19:34.319
a group assignment all by herself.

347
19:35.362 --> 19:38.240
Or the time she corrected the documents our instructor

348
19:38.323 --> 19:40.325
was submitting to the court.

349
19:40.409 --> 19:42.995
Those are quite amusing memories.

350
19:43.745 --> 19:46.248
Being with her makes me feel useless.

351
19:47.916 --> 19:50.460
I try to help her because I think she's in danger,

352
19:50.544 --> 19:52.713
but in the end, she wins and I lose.

353
19:53.839 --> 19:56.133
Never thought it'd be the same at work.

354
19:56.842 --> 20:00.095
I don't think she's much of a rival, though.

355
20:04.182 --> 20:05.684
Speak of the devil.

356
20:06.810 --> 20:08.937
She is bad with escalators.

357
20:10.897 --> 20:12.691
What should we do? Help her?

358
20:17.279 --> 20:19.114
I have a meeting with a client.

359
20:32.210 --> 20:34.129
The stairs are over there.

360
20:35.339 --> 20:36.298
I know.

361
20:37.257 --> 20:38.258
I see.

362
20:44.973 --> 20:46.975
I'm waiting for someone.

363
20:51.355 --> 20:53.023
Couldn't you get on the escalator

364
20:53.106 --> 20:55.067
if you just catch the timing?

365
20:57.402 --> 20:59.946
Try catching the rhythm.

366
21:08.538 --> 21:10.248
Give it a try next time.

367
21:13.043 --> 21:14.419
I need to make a call.

368
21:30.352 --> 21:31.520
Hello.

369
21:32.020 --> 21:33.313
Hello.

370
21:36.525 --> 21:40.404
I was told to guide the attorney to the hospital.

371
21:40.487 --> 21:42.906
I was told to wait for someone to guide me to the hospital.

372
21:43.740 --> 21:46.076
I apologize. You are the attorney.

373
21:47.577 --> 21:48.954
I'm Minami Minamida.

374
21:50.580 --> 21:52.499
Minami Minamida.

375
21:53.333 --> 21:54.793
I'm Funai, a paralegal.

376
21:55.377 --> 21:56.878
Well, shall we go?

377
22:00.298 --> 22:01.383
Want to try?

378
22:05.345 --> 22:06.680
Do you think I can?

379
22:07.264 --> 22:08.723
Please copy me.

380
22:27.242 --> 22:28.201
Exactly.

381
22:29.035 --> 22:30.036
Let's try it.

382
22:41.131 --> 22:42.299
Now!

383
22:54.519 --> 22:55.478
You did it! See?

384
22:56.771 --> 22:57.689
Yes.

385
22:58.273 --> 22:59.524
I did it!

386
23:05.697 --> 23:09.701
It feels like I'm diving deep into the bottom of the ocean!

387
23:43.360 --> 23:44.903
When getting off…

388
23:58.208 --> 23:59.084
Now.

389
24:01.836 --> 24:03.338
I did it!

390
24:03.421 --> 24:04.798
There you go!

391
24:09.970 --> 24:11.304
They look ridiculous.

392
24:15.684 --> 24:17.310
Under the dura mater here.

393
24:17.978 --> 24:19.562
What looks white is blood.

394
24:20.939 --> 24:23.650
Subdural hematomas are mainly caused by injuries.

395
24:25.694 --> 24:26.736
This is it, right?

396
24:26.820 --> 24:27.779
ISAO ICHINOSE

397
24:34.536 --> 24:35.704
Is something wrong?

398
24:36.538 --> 24:39.040
Sudden environment changes confuse me.

399
24:53.596 --> 24:54.848
He's sleeping right now.

400
24:55.473 --> 24:56.725
Shall we talk outside?

401
24:58.351 --> 24:59.185
Who is it?

402
24:59.269 --> 25:00.645
You're awake?

403
25:01.229 --> 25:02.689
Can you come over here?

404
25:02.772 --> 25:05.483
Honey, do you remember her?

405
25:06.443 --> 25:09.237
Little Minami who used to live in Unit 202.

406
25:09.863 --> 25:13.366
You know, her dad was at the University of Tokyo's law school.

407
25:14.075 --> 25:16.578
Minami is a lawyer now.

408
25:20.790 --> 25:21.958
Hello.

409
25:22.042 --> 25:24.210
I came to speak with you today.

410
25:27.005 --> 25:30.592
Also, could you sign this petition requesting leniency

411
25:30.675 --> 25:32.052
for the defendant?

412
25:34.012 --> 25:37.682
Are you that pervy four-eyes' daughter?

413
25:38.183 --> 25:39.017
Pervy four-eyes?

414
25:39.100 --> 25:40.727
Why are you here?

415
25:40.810 --> 25:42.103
And you, don't tell me…

416
25:42.187 --> 25:44.939
Are you still seeing that pervy four-eyes?

417
25:45.023 --> 25:46.983
-Hey, don't say weird things-- -Get out!

418
25:47.525 --> 25:49.361
Your old man is that pervy four-eyes.

419
25:50.028 --> 25:53.323
He made a move on my wife while I was out!

420
25:53.406 --> 25:54.574
Stop it already!

421
25:54.657 --> 25:55.575
Please calm down!

422
25:55.658 --> 25:57.494
-She is defending your wife. -Shut up!

423
25:58.453 --> 25:59.829
You bowl cut!

424
25:59.913 --> 26:02.540
Don't you ever show your face to me again!

425
26:03.500 --> 26:05.668
You hear me? Don't ever come back!

426
26:06.628 --> 26:09.089
Tell that to that pervy four-eyes, too!

427
26:17.263 --> 26:18.223
I'm sorry.

428
26:21.518 --> 26:25.355
My husband's always been paranoid.

429
26:27.357 --> 26:30.777
It has gotten worse since he developed dementia.

430
26:31.820 --> 26:34.114
If I have to see him like this,

431
26:34.697 --> 26:36.574
I should've just killed him then.

432
26:38.368 --> 26:40.745
Then, was your statement to the police

433
26:40.829 --> 26:44.040
that you wanted to kill your husband your true intention?

434
26:45.500 --> 26:48.211
Right now, yes. It is my true intention.

435
26:48.294 --> 26:49.671
What matters

436
26:49.754 --> 26:51.464
is how you felt then, not now.

437
26:53.758 --> 26:56.052
I don't know what to say.

438
26:57.053 --> 26:59.097
The law heavily weighs your feelings.

439
26:59.931 --> 27:02.142
Intending to kill means attempted murder.

440
27:02.225 --> 27:04.394
Intending to injure is assault.

441
27:04.477 --> 27:06.604
An accident is accidental injury.

442
27:08.106 --> 27:09.983
The charge changes based on your feelings.

443
27:14.112 --> 27:16.364
Human feelings are really difficult.

444
27:17.866 --> 27:19.325
I was taught

445
27:19.409 --> 27:22.537
that selfless acts are acts of compassion and love.

446
27:22.620 --> 27:24.038
Closing the blinds

447
27:24.122 --> 27:26.791
so it isn't too bright for someone sleeping

448
27:26.875 --> 27:28.251
is a selfless act.

449
27:28.334 --> 27:30.920
You don't do that for someone you want to kill.

450
27:33.923 --> 27:34.883
Am I wrong?

451
27:45.477 --> 27:47.562
CREATIVE RICE BALLS BEAMS

452
27:51.900 --> 27:54.360
MINAMI'S BEST FRIEND RIRII MADOKA

453
27:57.197 --> 27:58.281
I'm home.

454
27:58.364 --> 27:59.574
Welcome back.

455
27:59.657 --> 28:01.451
Minami!

456
28:02.702 --> 28:03.828
Minami to the Minamida

457
28:03.912 --> 28:05.330
Ririi to the Madoka

458
28:08.625 --> 28:10.793
My best friend had her first day at work,

459
28:10.877 --> 28:12.795
so I came to check on you!

460
28:12.879 --> 28:14.339
Thank you, Ririi.

461
28:14.422 --> 28:18.384
Can't believe you're braving the real world now.

462
28:19.052 --> 28:22.138
I need to hurry and make a living from my art, too.

463
28:22.222 --> 28:23.765
I like your art, Ririi.

464
28:23.848 --> 28:26.226
Until you can make a living, you can eat rice balls here.

465
28:26.309 --> 28:29.145
Here's the new tropical rice ball.

466
28:29.229 --> 28:31.439
For Minami, the Minami Minamida set.

467
28:31.523 --> 28:33.358
-Thanks, Mr. Minamida! -Here you go.

468
28:34.859 --> 28:36.277
-Let's eat. -Let's eat.

469
28:38.488 --> 28:39.489
By the way, Dad.

470
28:40.698 --> 28:42.408
Are you pervy four-eyes?

471
28:42.492 --> 28:44.452
What's this all of a sudden?

472
28:44.536 --> 28:46.621
Ms. Ichinose's husband said that.

473
28:47.205 --> 28:48.331
Ms. Ichinose?

474
28:48.957 --> 28:52.126
Of Unit 201 at Ocean Heim Nishikasai.

475
28:52.210 --> 28:53.378
That one?

476
28:53.461 --> 28:55.421
That you hit on his wife while he was out.

477
28:55.505 --> 28:57.131
No, I didn't.

478
28:57.215 --> 28:59.342
Her husband was just--

479
29:00.593 --> 29:02.470
Wait, how do you know her?

480
29:03.346 --> 29:04.472
That…

481
29:05.390 --> 29:06.808
I can't say due to confidentiality.

482
29:08.810 --> 29:10.854
Ririi, I have a trial coming up.

483
29:10.937 --> 29:13.189
A jury trial. I'll be arguing in front of everyone.

484
29:13.273 --> 29:14.607
That's awesome.

485
29:14.691 --> 29:15.692
She's having a trial?

486
29:15.775 --> 29:17.735
I can't say that either. It's confidential.

487
29:18.903 --> 29:21.823
I know! I'll draw you arguing in court

488
29:21.906 --> 29:23.283
to celebrate.

489
29:23.366 --> 29:25.285
Minami, strike a lawyer pose.

490
29:29.372 --> 29:30.206
Like this?

491
29:30.290 --> 29:31.332
Nice. Give it a line.

492
29:31.416 --> 29:32.876
-A line? -"Objection!"

493
29:33.835 --> 29:35.003
-Objection! -Make it bigger.

494
29:35.086 --> 29:37.630
-Objection! -Yes! Use your diaphragm!

495
29:37.714 --> 29:39.966
You are fined 100,000 yen!

496
29:40.049 --> 29:41.634
You are fined 100,000 yen!

497
29:42.886 --> 29:44.137
What did I do?

498
29:47.015 --> 29:49.017
COURTHOUSE

499
30:02.447 --> 30:03.448
FIRST HEARING

500
30:03.531 --> 30:05.575
Defense, your opening statement, please.

501
30:10.496 --> 30:12.540
Defense, what is the matter?

502
30:12.624 --> 30:13.791
Your opening statement.

503
30:15.251 --> 30:17.378
Ms. Minamida, the opening statement.

504
30:18.129 --> 30:19.547
What is wrong?

505
30:19.631 --> 30:20.465
Minami!

506
30:20.548 --> 30:21.591
RELAX, MINAMI!!

507
30:21.674 --> 30:22.675
Minami!

508
30:46.449 --> 30:48.117
Before my opening statement,

509
30:49.702 --> 30:51.037
I would like to say one thing.

510
30:52.497 --> 30:53.414
I have

511
30:54.749 --> 30:57.085
a disability called Autism Spectrum Disorder,

512
30:57.752 --> 30:59.045
and to you all,

513
30:59.754 --> 31:02.674
my way of speaking and my actions may seem unnatural.

514
31:03.341 --> 31:04.175
However,

515
31:05.760 --> 31:06.844
my love for the law

516
31:08.054 --> 31:10.348
and my respect for the defendant

517
31:10.431 --> 31:12.475
are no different from any other lawyer.

518
31:14.769 --> 31:15.895
As a defense attorney,

519
31:16.688 --> 31:18.022
I will do my absolute best

520
31:18.856 --> 31:21.776
to help the defendant and reveal the truth of this case.

521
31:31.619 --> 31:32.954
Order in the court!

522
31:35.707 --> 31:38.251
You love the law, do you?

523
31:40.169 --> 31:41.170
That is a good thing.

524
31:45.466 --> 31:46.300
DEFENDANT QUESTIONING

525
31:46.384 --> 31:48.177
"I'll kill you and then I'll die too."

526
31:49.512 --> 31:52.056
This is your statement to the police after the incident.

527
31:52.682 --> 31:55.018
There were police officers there at the time,

528
31:55.601 --> 31:58.479
so I got nervous and just said that.

529
31:59.439 --> 32:01.774
But I had no intention of killing him.

530
32:01.858 --> 32:03.735
Would someone who had no intention of killing

531
32:03.818 --> 32:05.945
talk about dying or ending it all?

532
32:06.029 --> 32:07.280
Objection!

533
32:07.363 --> 32:09.949
Leading the witness by assuming intent to kill.

534
32:10.033 --> 32:10.867
Sustained.

535
32:17.081 --> 32:19.042
Defense, please take your seat.

536
32:23.921 --> 32:27.717
This is the iron the defendant used when she attacked.

537
32:29.218 --> 32:30.178
Defendant.

538
32:30.928 --> 32:32.722
You hit him on the head with this,

539
32:33.264 --> 32:35.391
yet you truly had no intention of killing him?

540
32:36.017 --> 32:39.479
Didn't you actually want your husband dead?

541
32:39.562 --> 32:40.772
Objection.

542
32:40.855 --> 32:42.065
Leading the witness.

543
32:43.232 --> 32:44.275
Overruled.

544
32:46.277 --> 32:48.821
Defendant, please answer the question.

545
32:51.532 --> 32:53.910
I'm sorry, Your Honor.

546
32:56.120 --> 32:58.331
I devoted myself to my husband for so long,

547
32:59.332 --> 33:01.042
yet I was treated terribly,

548
33:03.044 --> 33:05.004
so I think I was feeling resentful.

549
33:07.090 --> 33:08.424
I'm so sorry.

550
33:10.885 --> 33:12.261
Please forgive me.

551
33:23.064 --> 33:26.150
That prosecutor was pretty tough.

552
33:26.234 --> 33:28.903
Next time, we'll be examining the victim as a witness.

553
33:28.986 --> 33:30.363
Then we'll have him testify

554
33:30.446 --> 33:32.406
that he doesn't want her punished.

555
33:32.490 --> 33:34.450
Will he be able to testify properly?

556
33:34.534 --> 33:36.035
He had quite a rough temper.

557
33:36.119 --> 33:38.621
The moment he saw Ms. Minamida, he started hurling abuse.

558
33:38.704 --> 33:40.581
Abuse? What did he say?

559
33:42.208 --> 33:43.668
He said, "You bowl cut."

560
33:43.751 --> 33:46.087
"Your old man is a pervy four-eyes."

561
33:46.170 --> 33:47.004
What on earth?

562
33:47.088 --> 33:50.133
He suspects that my father and the defendant had an affair.

563
33:51.509 --> 33:53.261
That does sound difficult.

564
33:54.053 --> 33:55.638
I asked the defendant

565
33:55.721 --> 33:58.266
and got the victim to sign a petition

566
33:58.349 --> 34:00.143
requesting no severe punishment,

567
34:00.226 --> 34:01.727
but should we submit it?

568
34:03.813 --> 34:05.189
What is this, a petition?

569
34:06.107 --> 34:07.191
No, don't submit it.

570
34:08.025 --> 34:10.778
I will handle the questioning, so draft up a script.

571
34:10.862 --> 34:12.446
Yes, understood.

572
34:27.670 --> 34:30.339
SECOND HEARING: WITNESS EXAMINATION

573
34:34.635 --> 34:36.637
Defense, proceed with the witness examination.

574
34:36.721 --> 34:37.680
Yes, Your Honor.

575
34:45.104 --> 34:46.772
Ms. Minamida, you go instead.

576
34:48.941 --> 34:50.651
Funai said so, right?

577
34:50.735 --> 34:52.862
That he hurled abuse the moment he saw you.

578
34:52.945 --> 34:54.280
Draw the abuse out of him.

579
34:57.408 --> 34:59.869
Defense, please proceed with the questioning.

580
34:59.952 --> 35:00.912
I am doing it now.

581
35:00.995 --> 35:02.079
Come on, hurry up.

582
35:04.749 --> 35:05.583
Yes.

583
35:16.344 --> 35:17.303
Hello.

584
35:17.386 --> 35:19.597
I'm Minami Minamida, your wife's attorney.

585
35:23.893 --> 35:25.019
You!

586
35:25.102 --> 35:27.188
Why are you here?

587
35:28.522 --> 35:29.815
You bowl cut!

588
35:29.899 --> 35:32.902
I told you never to show your face to me again!

589
35:32.985 --> 35:35.279
Witness, please calm down.

590
35:35.363 --> 35:37.615
Are you all in on this together?

591
35:38.199 --> 35:42.245
You set this up to watch me die of anger!

592
35:42.328 --> 35:45.706
Don't mess with me! You pieces of shit!

593
35:47.375 --> 35:50.294
Prosecutor, please escort the witness out of the courtroom.

594
35:52.213 --> 35:54.840
You call me out here and then do this?

595
35:54.924 --> 35:57.260
Stop making a fool out of me!

596
35:57.343 --> 36:00.721
Why are you like this? Making a fool of yourself in a place like this!

597
36:00.805 --> 36:02.765
Are you in on it, too?

598
36:02.848 --> 36:03.683
Let go of me!

599
36:05.059 --> 36:07.353
We will recess for ten minutes.

600
36:11.899 --> 36:12.733
Are you alright?

601
36:18.614 --> 36:20.283
We will now resume.

602
36:32.211 --> 36:34.171
As you just saw,

603
36:34.255 --> 36:37.008
the victim is a difficult person to live with.

604
36:38.175 --> 36:41.429
He becomes extremely suspicious of his wife and berates her.

605
36:41.512 --> 36:43.973
Despite this, the defendant

606
36:44.056 --> 36:45.683
supported her husband with dementia

607
36:45.766 --> 36:47.601
and cared for him devotedly.

608
36:48.602 --> 36:50.730
The defendant simply hit her husband

609
36:50.813 --> 36:52.356
impulsively out of sheer anger--

610
36:52.440 --> 36:53.691
Is something wrong?

611
36:53.774 --> 36:54.942
Over here.

612
37:03.284 --> 37:07.747
Your Honor, we have been informed the victim died while being transported.

613
37:07.830 --> 37:09.665
W-- What did you just say?

614
37:10.166 --> 37:11.459
My husband?

615
37:11.542 --> 37:13.544
My husband died…

616
37:15.713 --> 37:17.631
Therefore, we will consider

617
37:18.174 --> 37:19.759
changing the charge in this case

618
37:19.842 --> 37:22.303
from attempted murder to murder.

619
37:51.374 --> 37:52.958
Incense offering is this way.

620
37:57.254 --> 37:58.672
Mr. Miyaji.

621
37:59.632 --> 38:02.218
Please accept my deepest condolences.

622
38:02.301 --> 38:04.095
Thank you for coming all this way.

623
38:04.178 --> 38:05.179
Not at all.

624
38:06.972 --> 38:08.808
Thank you too, Minami.

625
38:12.978 --> 38:14.271
I…

626
38:17.483 --> 38:18.692
I'm sorry.

627
38:20.111 --> 38:22.071
It is because I made him angry…

628
38:23.364 --> 38:24.990
It's not your fault, Minami.

629
38:26.117 --> 38:29.078
It's because of his rough temper.

630
38:30.663 --> 38:31.622
Besides…

631
38:32.623 --> 38:34.291
I'm the one…

632
38:34.375 --> 38:36.836
who swung that iron around.

633
38:39.964 --> 38:41.424
It's my fault.

634
38:44.427 --> 38:46.429
I'm the one to blame.

635
39:00.985 --> 39:04.822
FUNERAL VENUE FOR THE LATE ISAO ICHINOSE

636
39:04.905 --> 39:06.824
It's unfortunate how things turned out.

637
39:08.617 --> 39:10.327
The responsibility is mine.

638
39:10.411 --> 39:12.746
Don't let it bother you, Ms. Minamida.

639
39:14.874 --> 39:18.335
With that said, I have decided

640
39:18.419 --> 39:21.755
to have Mr. Himi and Ms. Asahi take over this case.

641
39:24.675 --> 39:26.343
You must still be processing it.

642
39:27.178 --> 39:28.637
You can take a few days off.

643
39:30.556 --> 39:32.725
Yes, I understand.

644
40:03.255 --> 40:07.384
It seems you cannot even see whales in the dark ocean.

645
40:15.226 --> 40:16.060
I'm home.

646
40:16.143 --> 40:18.270
Welcome back, Minami. You're hungry, right?

647
40:18.354 --> 40:19.897
We got some really good salt.

648
40:19.980 --> 40:22.358
Which ocean was it from? Minami?

649
40:33.452 --> 40:34.328
Can I?

650
40:40.626 --> 40:42.628
I thought you'd prefer your usual salt.

651
40:43.963 --> 40:46.048
Here you go, the Minami Minamida set.

652
40:46.840 --> 40:49.343
Being hungry keeps your mood down, too.

653
40:52.179 --> 40:54.557
Why did I become a lawyer?

654
40:56.183 --> 40:57.017
What's this now?

655
40:57.601 --> 41:00.145
My boss asked me that on my first day.

656
41:02.273 --> 41:03.357
I…

657
41:04.858 --> 41:06.819
I couldn't even answer that.

658
41:09.321 --> 41:10.906
Because I'm good at memorizing?

659
41:11.740 --> 41:13.284
Because I passed the bar?

660
41:15.411 --> 41:17.788
I remember everything I've ever read,

661
41:18.539 --> 41:20.124
but I can't ride an escalator alone.

662
41:23.377 --> 41:26.171
Maybe being a lawyer

663
41:26.880 --> 41:29.049
was impossible for me with autism after all.

664
41:40.185 --> 41:41.270
You know, Minami,

665
41:43.022 --> 41:45.149
any parent has at least one day

666
41:45.983 --> 41:49.486
where they think, "Maybe my kid is special."

667
41:51.905 --> 41:53.907
It's been almost 20 years now, I guess.

668
41:55.534 --> 41:56.744
I had…

669
41:57.411 --> 41:58.662
a day like that, too.

670
42:00.497 --> 42:01.373
Minami.

671
42:04.460 --> 42:05.878
Minami Minamida.

672
42:09.673 --> 42:12.009
Most of the time when I talk to her, she's like this.

673
42:13.093 --> 42:14.845
She hasn't spoken any words yet.

674
42:15.429 --> 42:18.057
Your daughter may have autism.

675
42:19.725 --> 42:21.518
Autism…

676
42:26.732 --> 42:27.858
Hey, Minami.

677
42:28.442 --> 42:31.153
Do you know who Dad is?

678
42:38.535 --> 42:39.620
Hey… Minami!

679
42:47.711 --> 42:48.629
Minami.

680
42:48.712 --> 42:51.131
-Hey, I've been waiting for you. -H-- Hey, what is it?

681
42:51.215 --> 42:53.258
You! You made a move on my wife, didn't you?

682
42:53.342 --> 42:56.053
Hey, please stop! Hey!

683
42:56.136 --> 42:58.806
What were you doing while I was out?

684
42:58.889 --> 43:01.308
What on earth were you doing with my wife?

685
43:01.392 --> 43:03.560
What on earth? My kid's watching! Stop it!

686
43:03.644 --> 43:05.229
What were you doing?

687
43:06.772 --> 43:08.691
Hey, what are you doing?

688
43:09.358 --> 43:10.317
Please, stop!

689
43:11.110 --> 43:12.319
I was working,

690
43:12.403 --> 43:14.363
so I just had your wife look after my daughter.

691
43:14.446 --> 43:16.573
Looking at my wife with those pervy eyes.

692
43:16.657 --> 43:19.034
-You pervy four eyes! -Please stop.

693
43:19.118 --> 43:20.786
-Hey! -The crime of bodily injury.

694
43:23.122 --> 43:25.290
A person who inflicts bodily injury upon another

695
43:25.374 --> 43:29.837
shall face up to ten years in prison or a 300,000 yen fine.

696
43:30.713 --> 43:31.547
Minami?

697
43:35.718 --> 43:36.885
Did you hear that?

698
43:36.969 --> 43:38.303
-You heard that, right? -Yes!

699
43:38.387 --> 43:39.304
Minami spoke!

700
43:39.388 --> 43:40.472
"Crime of bodily injury!"

701
43:43.559 --> 43:44.935
Minami!

702
43:46.437 --> 43:47.438
You can speak.

703
43:48.397 --> 43:49.773
You can, Minami!

704
43:52.943 --> 43:54.945
Where did you learn that?

705
43:56.697 --> 43:57.740
Could it be…

706
43:57.823 --> 43:58.907
Wait here a second.

707
44:02.536 --> 44:05.122
Little Minami!

708
44:10.085 --> 44:12.171
Was it from here?

709
44:12.254 --> 44:13.630
The crime of bodily injury.

710
44:14.256 --> 44:16.008
A person who inflicts bodily injury

711
44:16.091 --> 44:19.803
upon another shall face up to ten years in prison or a 300,000 yen fine.

712
44:19.887 --> 44:21.263
It all matches.

713
44:23.390 --> 44:24.933
Wonderful!

714
44:25.017 --> 44:26.977
She's a genius!

715
44:27.060 --> 44:29.730
That's why she's a little different from other kids.

716
44:29.813 --> 44:34.860
Minami, you should become a lawyer when you grow up.

717
44:35.778 --> 44:36.779
Yes!

718
44:36.862 --> 44:37.863
She will!

719
44:39.573 --> 44:40.783
The crime of bodily injury.

720
44:41.825 --> 44:42.993
Since then, Minami,

721
44:43.076 --> 44:45.913
you've stared at the compendium of laws every day.

722
44:49.124 --> 44:51.251
COMPENDIUM OF LAWS

723
44:55.714 --> 44:59.885
So that was my motivation for trying to become a lawyer.

724
45:00.969 --> 45:03.096
At that moment, I realized

725
45:03.180 --> 45:05.432
that you really had

726
45:05.974 --> 45:07.851
your own world inside you.

727
45:15.317 --> 45:16.401
Minami?

728
45:17.069 --> 45:18.278
Your rice balls?

729
45:27.162 --> 45:29.164
Go get 'em, Minami!

730
45:32.709 --> 45:34.628
Ms. Minamida, did you forget something here?

731
45:34.711 --> 45:36.964
No, I didn't forget anything.

732
45:43.679 --> 45:45.472
-Mr. Funai. -Yes.

733
45:47.057 --> 45:48.684
The very first word I spoke

734
45:48.767 --> 45:51.353
when I was four was "the crime of bodily injury."

735
45:51.937 --> 45:55.566
And the first person who told me I should become a lawyer

736
45:55.649 --> 45:57.359
was Mr. Ichinose's wife.

737
45:58.110 --> 45:59.027
Right.

738
45:59.111 --> 46:00.904
I just found out and was surprised.

739
46:01.697 --> 46:05.325
And the first trial I'm in charge of is for that same Keiko Ichinose.

740
46:05.409 --> 46:06.743
And the key to this trial

741
46:06.827 --> 46:10.205
is whether we can reduce her charge to the crime of bodily injury.

742
46:10.914 --> 46:12.499
That's why I…

743
46:14.668 --> 46:16.878
In other words, are you saying you want

744
46:16.962 --> 46:18.922
to handle this case until the very end?

745
46:20.799 --> 46:22.009
Yes!

746
46:22.092 --> 46:24.761
I'm saying I want to handle this case until the very end.

747
46:33.395 --> 46:34.229
Yes?

748
46:34.896 --> 46:35.814
Excuse me.

749
46:36.440 --> 46:38.400
The victim's death certificate arrived.

750
46:38.483 --> 46:40.068
You might want to take a look.

751
46:40.277 --> 46:41.570
Yes, I will take a look.

752
46:42.821 --> 46:44.656
DEATH CERTIFICATE

753
46:44.740 --> 46:47.993
Cause of death was indeed a recurrence of the subdural hematoma.

754
46:54.333 --> 46:57.169
It's a miracle he didn't die instantly after being hit

755
46:57.252 --> 46:58.587
on the head with this.

756
46:59.630 --> 47:01.214
Doesn't this iron look like that…

757
47:01.298 --> 47:03.008
-From Pinocchio… -A sperm whale.

758
47:03.091 --> 47:04.676
Yes! A sperm whale.

759
47:05.510 --> 47:07.512
This part here looks like the shape of its head.

760
47:12.893 --> 47:13.727
What is it?

761
47:18.148 --> 47:21.193
There are many things I'm not allowed to do at work.

762
47:21.276 --> 47:23.195
Echolalia, weird remarks.

763
47:23.278 --> 47:25.238
Kayak, deed, rotator, civic, racecar.

764
47:25.322 --> 47:27.366
Also, speaking too honestly.

765
47:27.908 --> 47:28.742
Is that so?

766
47:28.825 --> 47:31.328
Especially talking about whales. That's forbidden.

767
47:31.411 --> 47:32.788
Unless it's absolutely necessary.

768
47:33.455 --> 47:34.581
I'll be careful.

769
47:35.415 --> 47:38.043
Even if the iron looks like a sperm whale…

770
47:55.602 --> 47:58.730
Seeing the iron as a sperm whale

771
47:58.814 --> 48:01.024
made me miss that they don't lay eggs!

772
48:01.108 --> 48:02.067
What?

773
48:03.068 --> 48:06.238
In this case, civil law is relevant, not criminal law.

774
48:06.321 --> 48:09.324
Likewise, we can't judge it by the iron alone.

775
48:10.867 --> 48:11.743
The petition?

776
48:13.286 --> 48:14.329
The signature.

777
48:15.414 --> 48:17.165
Maybe there's an eyewitness.

778
48:18.667 --> 48:19.543
What?

779
48:23.046 --> 48:23.880
COURTHOUSE

780
48:23.964 --> 48:25.674
Let's proceed with cross-examination.

781
48:25.757 --> 48:27.050
3RD HEARING: WITNESS EXAMINATION

782
48:27.134 --> 48:28.135
Yes, Your Honor!

783
48:29.511 --> 48:33.640
Subdural hematomas include traumatic ones caused by injuries

784
48:33.724 --> 48:36.393
and non-traumatic ones caused by illness.

785
48:36.476 --> 48:37.644
Is that correct?

786
48:37.728 --> 48:38.562
Yes.

787
48:38.645 --> 48:40.147
According to your diagnosis,

788
48:40.230 --> 48:42.566
the victim had no skull fractures

789
48:42.649 --> 48:44.484
and the head wound was shallow.

790
48:44.568 --> 48:45.485
Yes.

791
48:45.569 --> 48:47.529
Could the victim

792
48:47.612 --> 48:49.906
have had a non-traumatic subdural hematoma

793
48:49.990 --> 48:51.366
before the iron hit him?

794
48:51.450 --> 48:53.285
Before the iron hit him?

795
48:53.368 --> 48:54.202
For instance…

796
48:56.997 --> 49:00.125
Exactly when the defendant swung the iron,

797
49:00.208 --> 49:03.712
the victim collapsed due to a non-traumatic subdural hematoma.

798
49:03.795 --> 49:05.422
Is there no possibility of that?

799
49:05.505 --> 49:08.967
Objection. Counsel is seeking the witness's opinion, not asking a question.

800
49:09.968 --> 49:11.178
Sustained.

801
49:11.261 --> 49:14.014
Defense, please only ask questions.

802
49:14.097 --> 49:15.223
Only ask questions.

803
49:15.307 --> 49:16.141
What?

804
49:29.529 --> 49:31.406
Mr. Isao was 81.

805
49:31.490 --> 49:33.658
He suffered from dementia.

806
49:33.742 --> 49:37.245
Non-traumatic subdural hematomas are common in the elderly

807
49:37.329 --> 49:39.790
and dementia patients. Correct?

808
49:39.873 --> 49:40.916
Well,

809
49:40.999 --> 49:44.586
if there were warning signs or symptoms, it would be a different story,

810
49:44.669 --> 49:48.340
but we can't confirm a non-traumatic hematoma on that alone.

811
49:49.174 --> 49:52.511
It would be a different story if there were warning signs?

812
49:52.594 --> 49:53.804
Well, yes.

813
50:00.811 --> 50:02.312
Thank you.

814
50:05.148 --> 50:07.067
Witness, you delivered a package

815
50:07.150 --> 50:10.278
to the Ichinose residence on the day of the incident, correct?

816
50:10.529 --> 50:11.363
Yes.

817
50:11.446 --> 50:13.490
Who first answered the door

818
50:13.573 --> 50:15.492
when you delivered the package?

819
50:16.076 --> 50:17.869
Ms. Ichinose's husband.

820
50:20.205 --> 50:22.958
This is a copy of the delivery slip from that time.

821
50:28.296 --> 50:30.715
Whose signature is this in the receipt section?

822
50:31.299 --> 50:32.676
Ms. Ichinose.

823
50:36.388 --> 50:38.807
Why didn't you get Mr. Isao's signature?

824
50:39.516 --> 50:41.268
I tried to, but…

825
50:43.144 --> 50:44.980
My head feels like it's splitting.

826
50:45.063 --> 50:47.190
Package here. Can I get a signature?

827
50:47.274 --> 50:48.191
Yeah.

828
50:51.987 --> 50:53.488
My fingers are numb.

829
50:54.406 --> 50:56.491
-Are you okay? -Shut up!

830
50:56.575 --> 50:58.910
Hey, a package arrived.

831
50:59.411 --> 51:00.996
You sign for it.

832
51:05.709 --> 51:06.835
Looking at the slip,

833
51:06.918 --> 51:11.131
there's a messy line here protruding from the signature box.

834
51:12.757 --> 51:16.928
There's no doubt that this was written by her husband, Mr. Isao,

835
51:17.012 --> 51:19.389
when he tried to sign, correct?

836
51:20.640 --> 51:22.475
Objection! Leading the witness.

837
51:22.559 --> 51:23.602
Overruled.

838
51:23.685 --> 51:25.437
Witness, what is your answer?

839
51:31.568 --> 51:32.944
That's correct.

840
51:36.573 --> 51:37.532
Your Honor!

841
51:38.241 --> 51:41.453
Before the incident, the victim had numbness in his fingertips

842
51:41.536 --> 51:43.413
and couldn't even write a signature.

843
51:43.496 --> 51:45.624
Furthermore, he complained of a headache.

844
51:46.333 --> 51:49.920
These can be called warning signs of a non-traumatic subdural hematoma.

845
51:50.629 --> 51:53.506
In other words, the subdural hematoma

846
51:53.590 --> 51:56.176
may not have been caused by the defendant's assault,

847
51:56.259 --> 51:58.637
but by his pre-existing illness!

848
51:58.720 --> 52:00.513
I'll kill you…

849
52:01.598 --> 52:03.642
And then I'll die too!

850
52:03.725 --> 52:05.477
This is the end.

851
52:09.689 --> 52:12.317
In criminal trials, there is a fundamental principle

852
52:12.400 --> 52:15.111
that the defendant gets the benefit of the doubt.

853
52:15.904 --> 52:19.699
Since his pre-existing illness may have caused his death…

854
52:19.783 --> 52:21.660
Unless the prosecution

855
52:21.743 --> 52:23.995
can medically prove a causal relationship

856
52:24.079 --> 52:27.082
between the defendant's strike and the resulting death…

857
52:28.249 --> 52:30.210
The defendant cannot be held

858
52:30.293 --> 52:32.879
criminally responsible for the death itself!

859
52:37.550 --> 52:41.638
It seems we will need to re-examine this matter.

860
52:52.107 --> 52:53.400
That is all.

861
53:04.911 --> 53:07.247
It depends on the prosecution's proof,

862
53:07.330 --> 53:10.500
but you'll likely get a suspended sentence for bodily injury.

863
53:11.501 --> 53:13.086
Thank you.

864
53:17.674 --> 53:18.925
Ms. Minamida.

865
53:20.260 --> 53:21.261
You did a good job.

866
53:22.679 --> 53:24.139
Yes. I did a good job.

867
53:27.434 --> 53:28.560
Ms. Minamida.

868
53:31.354 --> 53:32.689
It's all thanks to you.

869
53:34.566 --> 53:36.443
Thank you so much.

870
53:41.865 --> 53:43.324
Thank you.

871
54:16.649 --> 54:18.068
Thank you very much.

872
54:18.526 --> 54:19.486
What?

873
54:20.528 --> 54:23.114
Thanks to you thinking it through with me,

874
54:23.198 --> 54:26.034
I realized the iron didn't cause a fatal wound.

875
54:26.868 --> 54:29.913
It's all thanks to you. You fought for your client.

876
54:32.457 --> 54:33.708
About that thing…

877
54:35.043 --> 54:36.169
That thing?

878
54:36.252 --> 54:37.545
Talking about whales.

879
54:37.629 --> 54:39.964
Isn't it fine when it's just the two of us?

880
54:41.257 --> 54:42.133
What?

881
54:43.635 --> 54:44.761
Is it really okay?

882
54:45.261 --> 54:46.596
I don't mind.

883
54:47.597 --> 54:49.390
To talk about whales?

884
54:49.474 --> 54:50.767
Yes.

885
54:52.602 --> 54:54.854
When it's just you and me, Mr. Funai?

886
54:54.938 --> 54:57.273
Yeah. When it's just the two of us.

887
55:02.737 --> 55:04.072
Thank you!

888
55:08.868 --> 55:09.911
Are you okay?

889
55:11.162 --> 55:13.748
I don't know where to start.

890
55:14.833 --> 55:17.377
First, let's talk about sperm whales!

891
55:18.294 --> 55:19.129
Okay.

892
55:21.214 --> 55:23.049
Most female sperm whales

893
55:23.133 --> 55:25.385
spend their entire lives in the same pod.

894
55:25.468 --> 55:27.887
Males leave the pod around age ten

895
55:27.971 --> 55:30.890
and form pods with other young adult males.

896
55:30.974 --> 55:34.018
As they mature further, they begin to travel alone.

897
55:43.278 --> 55:45.113
Sorry. We're closed for today--

898
55:50.118 --> 55:51.077
Long time no see.

899
56:03.756 --> 56:05.842
Her wedding dress slipped down

900
56:05.925 --> 56:07.552
during the ceremony…

901
56:07.635 --> 56:09.512
How much do you think that ceremony cost?

902
56:09.596 --> 56:11.055
The husband loves his wife--

903
56:11.848 --> 56:14.017
Let's go undercover for this one.

904
56:14.100 --> 56:16.978
My, my, the groom is completely captivated.

905
56:17.061 --> 56:17.937
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
